yes - repeat a line

SYNOPSIS
    yes [argument ...]

DESCRIPTION
    Write a line repeatedly to standard output until it closes or the
    process is interrupted. The arguments are separated by single spaces.
    With no arguments, the line contains y.

EXAMPLES
    yes hello | head -3

SEE ALSO
    echo(1), head(1), seq(1)
